      {"q":"Which blood cells carry oxygen around the body?","o":["White blood cells","Platelets","Red blood cells","Nerve cells"],"a":2,"e":"Red blood cells hold haemoglobin, an iron rich protein that grabs oxygen in the lungs."},
      {"q":"What causes the sound of thunder?","o":["Rain hitting the ground hard","Air heated by lightning expanding fast","Clouds banging into each other","Wind rushing between two clouds"],"a":1,"e":"Lightning heats the air to thousands of degrees at once, and that air blasts outward as a shock wave."},
      {"q":"What is the chemical symbol for gold?","o":["Ag","Au","Gd","Go"],"a":1,"e":"It comes from aurum, the old Latin name for gold, so the letters do not match the modern word."},
      {"q":"Which part of a cell holds its DNA?","o":["The cell wall","The cytoplasm","The membrane","The nucleus"],"a":3,"e":"The nucleus works like a safe, keeping the instructions for the whole cell in one protected place."},
      {"q":"Which organ filters waste out of the blood to make urine?","o":["The liver","The kidneys","The lungs","The stomach"],"a":1,"e":"Blood passes through the kidneys many times a day so waste and extra water can be removed."},
      {"q":"Why does a straw look bent where it enters a glass of water?","o":["The water pushes the straw sideways","The glass is never truly flat","Light bends when it passes into water","Water makes plastic soften slightly"],"a":2,"e":"Light slows down in water and changes direction, an effect called refraction."},
      {"q":"What is the general word for rain, snow, sleet and hail?","o":["Precipitation","Condensation","Evaporation","Humidity"],"a":0,"e":"Precipitation covers any water that falls out of a cloud, whether it lands liquid or frozen."},
      {"q":"On the pH scale, which number means a liquid is neutral?","o":["0","7","10","14"],"a":1,"e":"Below that number a liquid is acidic and above it a liquid is basic, so pure water sits in the middle."},
      {"q":"Sound travels fastest through which of these?","o":["Air","Steel","Water","Empty space"],"a":1,"e":"Sound moves by shaking particles, and the tightly packed particles of a solid pass the shake along quickest."}
