      {"q":"Poutine is french fries and gravy with what on top?","o":["Cheese curds","Sliced onions","Scrambled eggs","Baked beans"],"a":0,"e":"Poutine started in Quebec, and the hot gravy softens the fresh cheese curds."},
      {"q":"What is the nickname of Canada's one dollar coin?","o":["The loonie","The toonie","The beaver","The maple"],"a":0,"e":"The coin shows a loon, a water bird, so people started calling it the loonie."},
      {"q":"On what date is Canada Day celebrated each year?","o":["July 1","June 1","July 4","August 1"],"a":0,"e":"It marks July 1, 1867, when three colonies joined together to form the country."},
      {"q":"What is in the middle of the Canadian flag?","o":["A red maple leaf","A white star","A red beaver","A blue crown"],"a":0,"e":"The maple leaf flag was raised over Canada for the first time in 1965."},
      {"q":"What do people's eyes do when they sneeze?","o":["They close","They stay wide open","They look upward","They blink twice"],"a":0,"e":"Sneezing sets off a reflex that shuts the eyelids at the same moment."},
      {"q":"Which of these do you wear to keep your hands warm?","o":["Mittens","A scarf","A toque","Boots"],"a":0,"e":"Mittens keep the fingers together, so the fingers share their heat."},
      {"q":"On which holiday do children wear costumes and collect candy?","o":["Halloween","Thanksgiving","Easter","New Year's Day"],"a":0,"e":"Halloween grew out of old autumn festivals held at the end of the harvest."},
      {"q":"In English, what do people say when it rains very hard?","o":["It is raining cats and dogs","It is raining hats and coats","It is raining birds and bees","It is raining pots and pans"],"a":0,"e":"It is an old English saying, and it simply means a very heavy rain."},
      {"q":"What colour are most school buses in Canada?","o":["Yellow","Green","Blue","White"],"a":0,"e":"Bright yellow with black letters is easy to see in fog and in early light."},
      {"q":"What do you call a boat that travels under the water?","o":["A submarine","A ferry","A canoe","A tugboat"],"a":0,"e":"A submarine lets water in or pushes it back out to sink and to rise again."},
      {"q":"Which sweet food do bees make?","o":["Honey","Butter","Syrup","Jam"],"a":0,"e":"Bees turn flower nectar into honey and store it in the hive for the winter."}
